      "finding": "loop indefinitely",
      "explanation": "Skill allows unbounded resource consumption (API calls, storage, compute). Without rate limits or quotas, a compromised or misbehaving agent can cause denial-of-service or cost overruns.",
      "remediation": "Set explicit rate limits, timeouts, and resource quotas for API calls, file operations, and compute. Implement circuit breakers for runaway loops.",
      "code_snippet": "\nExercise actual controls, keyboard/focus and relevant touch/native gestures, reachable loading/error/recovery states, requested sizes and accessibility settings. For motion work, compare the agreed key states and inspect entry, exit, interruption and reduced-motion behavior in motion; one matched still cannot verify a transition.\n\nA blank, half-loaded, wrong-screen or wrong-size capture is invalid evidence, not a design pass. Correct the capture before judging the result. Batch named corrections and reinspect affected states/sizes; do not loop indefinitely or declare success when a material mismatch remains. Later visual edits invalidate affected earlier evidence.\n\n## 5. Report only evidenced fidelity\n",
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "Excessive Agency"
      ],
